# Purpose: Recursively replace values whose object keys contain (case-insensitively) password, token, secret, credential, private[_ -]?key, api[_ -]?key, or authorization. This key-name filter does not sanitize free text, and values under unmatched keys are not guaranteed secret-free.
# Inputs: fixtures/052/service-response.json contains a synthetic service response. Supported case-insensitive key patterns are password, token, secret, credential, private[_ -]?key, api[_ -]?key, and authorization; unmatched keys and free text are not guaranteed secret-free.
# Outputs: Compact JSON with sensitive values replaced by a redaction marker.
accept service_response_path as text with default "fixtures/052/service-response.json"
run cat with path service_response_path
then jq with filter "def redact: if type == \"object\" then with_entries(if (.key | ascii_downcase | test(\"password|token|secret|credential|private[ _-]?key|api[ _-]?key|authorization\")) then .value = \"[REDACTED]\" else .value |= redact end) elif type == \"array\" then map(redact) else . end; redact" and flags ["-c", "-S"]
